-- Children's Court of Western Australia Act 1988 (WA), ss 3, 19-23, 28, 31, 33-36A, 40 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_children-s-court-of-western-australia-act-1988_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts are from the workbench scenario au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake/facts.json (Jake born 30 August 2006), as in
-- the Young Offenders Act 1994 baseline. Jake was referred to a juvenile justice team and never charged; the charge
-- fixtures say what would happen if he had been. The hearing date of 1 February 2022 is ASSUMED. That stealing worth
-- $89 is an indictable offence that may be tried summarily is read from The Criminal Code ss 5, 378 and 426(4).

